[IQ Generator Preset]
# Lesson 8: oscillator phase noise.
# A free-running oscillator makes the phase random-walk, smearing each 16-QAM point into an arc instead of a round cloud. Compare with lesson 6, where AWGN spreads points radially. The phase wanders more the longer the signal runs, and the outer points blur first. Raise the linewidth to 0.1 Hz and the clouds become full rings. Use the Constellation tab with the matched-filter view.
Version=3
Modulation=16-QAM
NumberOfSymbols=1024
SymbolRateBaud=1000
SamplesPerSymbol=8
Pulse=RRC
RRCBeta=0.2
SpanSymbols=10
AmplitudeGain=1
DataSource=Random
Seed=5489
Bits=
